# Add contrast to owner corner triangles

Draw a visible boundary along each All-player ownership triangle's hypotenuse so the marker remains legible over white row content.

## Acceptance criteria

- [x] Every owner triangle shown in All-player mode has a line exactly along its diagonal/hypotenuse.
- [x] The diagonal uses sufficient contrast to remain visible for the white player marker on a light row background.
- [x] The line remains visually appropriate for red, blue, orange, white, green, and purple markers.
- [x] The triangle fill continues to use the owning player's colour.
- [x] The line and triangle stay within the upper-right corner of the fixed left-hand cell.
- [x] The change does not alter row height, icon/name alignment, expansion, or fixed/value-pane synchronization.
- [x] Single-player mode continues to hide owner markers entirely.
- [x] Existing ownership accessibility labels remain available without introducing a duplicate row action.
- [x] Rendering and UI regression coverage compile.
- [ ] Focused light/dark appearance checks pass on a functioning simulator or device.

## Scope notes

- This task refines TASK-036; it does not change ownership storage or filtering.

## Evidence

- Added a dedicated inset hypotenuse path over the unchanged 13-point owner triangle.
- Used adaptive primary colour at 65% opacity for contrast in light and dark appearances, including white ownership.
- Updated SCR-002 while preserving marker layout and accessibility behavior.
